  topic: Federal Funding Update (Dr. Prince)
  desc: Dr. Johanna Prince, Assistant Superintendent, provided an update on federal
    funding from the Elementary and Secondary Education Act (ESEA), also known as
    Title Funds. She explained the four main titles (Title I, IIA, III, IV) and their
    purposes.
  children:
  - seconds: 3407
    speaker: Dr. Prince
    text: Dr. Prince explained that Title I targets students from lower socioeconomic
      backgrounds, Title IIA supports professional development, Title III aids multilingual
      students, and Title IV covers student support and academic enrichment. She noted
      that funds can be combined to support projects.
  - seconds: 3475
    speaker: Dr. Prince
    text: Dr. Prince reported a significant decrease of almost $150,000 in South Portland's
      federal funding for FY25, primarily in Title I, due to a lower state allocation
      and new guidance for charter school allocations. She emphasized the importance
      of considering this for the FY26 budget to maintain support for Kaler and Skillin.
  - seconds: 3608
    speaker: Dr. Prince
    text: Dr. Prince detailed the allocation of funds, with 65% going to Skillin and
      the rest to Kaler for math literacy and intervention roles. These funds also
      support a regular education social work position (4/5 Skillin, 1/5 Kaler) and
      a behavior strategist across four elementary schools.
  - seconds: 3695
    speaker: Dr. Prince
    text: Dr. Prince explained that $65,000 supports multilingual students, funding
      supplemental programming and specialists, and professional development. She
      also mentioned setting aside $25,000 for professional learning from Title II
      funds and outlined allocations for non-public schools (Holy Cross, Greater Portland
      Christian Academy, Portland Kids Academy).
